---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const repoUrl = 'https://krabka-io.github.io/charts';

const addRepo = `helm repo add krabka ${repoUrl}
helm repo update
helm search repo krabka`;

const install = `helm install krabka-operator krabka/krabka-operator \\
  --namespace krabka-system --create-namespace`;

const keyUid = 'Krabka Charts <charts@krabka.dev>';
const keyFingerprint = '74A6 7D5C F9AE 199A 45D2  2E42 594B D543 4544 D339';

const verify = `# Import the chart signing public key, then check the fingerprint
# against the one published on this page before you trust it.
gpg --import krabka-charts.pub.asc
gpg --fingerprint charts@krabka.dev

# Helm needs a binary keyring, not an armored file.
gpg --export charts@krabka.dev > krabka-keyring.gpg

helm install krabka-operator krabka/krabka-operator \\
  --verify --keyring ./krabka-keyring.gpg`;

const charts = [
  { name: 'krabka-operator', repo: 'krabka-operator', purpose: 'The Kubernetes operator. It reconciles Kafka, KafkaNodePool, KafkaTopic, KafkaUser, KafkaRebalance and SchemaRegistry resources.' },
  { name: 'krabka-rebalancer', repo: 'krabka-rebalancer', purpose: 'The partition rebalancer. It answers KafkaRebalance requests with a partition assignment plan.' },
  { name: 'krabka-schema-registry', repo: 'krabka-schema-registry', purpose: 'The Confluent-API-compatible schema registry. It stores schemas in the compacted _schemas topic.' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Helm Chart Repository"
  description="One Helm repository URL for every Krabka chart. The site aggregates the charts published by the component repositories into a single index.yaml."
  currentSlug="/docs/helm-charts"
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Helm Chart Repository</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-base">
        One repository URL for every Krabka chart.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Krabka charts are built in the repository that owns each component. The site aggregates them
        into one Helm repository, so you add a single URL and get every chart from it.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose bg-black/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 relative font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center text-gray-400 mb-2 font-sans">
          <span>Add the repository:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn flex items-center gap-1 rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-all font-sans" data-copy={addRepo}>
            <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z" /></svg>
            <span>Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre class="text-krab-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>{addRepo}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Charts in the index</h2>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
          <thead class="bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-white/10 uppercase text-gray-400 font-sans">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Chart</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Source repository</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">What it installs</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 font-sans">
            {charts.map((c) => (
              <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-white text-xs whitespace-nowrap">{c.name}</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4">
                  <a class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300" href={`https://github.com/krabka-io/${c.repo}`}>
                    krabka-io/{c.repo}
                  </a>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">{c.purpose}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        <a class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300" href={`${repoUrl}/index.yaml`}>index.yaml</a>
        is the authoritative list. A component repository joins the index as soon as it holds a
        <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">charts/</code> directory, so the table above can lag the
        index by a release.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Install a chart</h2>

      <div class="not-prose bg-black/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 relative font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center text-gray-400 mb-2 font-sans">
          <span>Install the operator:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn flex items-center gap-1 rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-all font-sans" data-copy={install}>
            <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z" /></svg>
            <span>Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre class="text-krab-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>{install}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Verify a chart</h2>
      <p>
        The charts carry a Helm provenance file when the release job has the signing key. The public
        half of that key lives in
        <a class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300" href="https://github.com/krabka-io/tooling">krabka-io/tooling</a>,
        under <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">charts/</code>. It is never stored on this site.
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl border border-white/10 p-4 not-prose space-y-1.5">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 font-sans">Chart signing key</div>
        <div class="font-mono text-sm text-white">{keyUid}</div>
        <div class="font-mono text-xs text-krab-300 break-all">{keyFingerprint}</div>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 pt-1">
          Check this fingerprint against the key you import. Any earlier Krabka chart key is revoked
          and must not be used.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose bg-black/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 relative font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center text-gray-400 mb-2 font-sans">
          <span>Verify before install:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn flex items-center gap-1 rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-all font-sans" data-copy={verify}>
            <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z" /></svg>
            <span>Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre class="text-krab-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>{verify}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">How the index is built</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-gray-300">
        <li>A scheduled job in this repository walks the krabka-io organisation.</li>
        <li>It takes every repository that holds a <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">charts/</code> directory.</li>
        <li>It packages each chart at the version in that repository's workspace <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">Cargo.toml</code>.</li>
        <li>It writes one <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">index.yaml</code> over the whole set and commits it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        The index holds the current version of each chart. A renamed chart drops out under its old
        name on the next run. A component repository can ask for an immediate rebuild by sending a
        <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">charts-changed</code> repository dispatch to this
        repository.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
